From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:04:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ipv6: register the optr sysctl in the initial namespace only

MediaTek's VzW change (c4547675d3b1, "ipv6: VzW requirement for ipv6")
registers net/optr from ipv6_sysctl_net_init(), so in every network
namespace, but keeps the header only in a local variable.
ipv6_sysctl_net_exit() never unregisters it, so each namespace that goes
away leaks the table and trips the check in retire_sysctl_set():

  WARNING: CPU: 3 PID: 8471 at retire_sysctl_set+0x24/0x30
  Workqueue: netns ...
  Call trace:
   retire_sysctl_set+0x24/0x30
   sysctl_net_exit+0x10/0x18
   cleanup_net+0x3ac/0x574

On LuneOS that is every systemd service with PrivateNetwork= and every
"unshare -n": one boot logged it eleven times.

The entry points at sysctl_optr, a single global, so a copy per
namespace only ever gave each namespace another handle on the same
integer. Register it in init_net, which is never torn down, and nowhere
else. Keeping a per-namespace header for the exit path instead would
need a new field in struct net.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [MediaTek vendor change, exists only in the vendor tree]
---
 net/ipv6/sysctl_net_ipv6.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/ipv6/sysctl_net_ipv6.c b/net/ipv6/sysctl_net_ipv6.c
index e0519c64e6f1..3a3d310fb0fd 100644
--- a/net/ipv6/sysctl_net_ipv6.c
+++ b/net/ipv6/sysctl_net_ipv6.c
@@ -251,9 +251,16 @@ static int __net_init ipv6_sysctl_net_init(struct net *net)
 	if (!net->ipv6.sysctl.hdr)
 		goto out_ipv6_icmp_table;
 
-	vzw_hdr = register_net_sysctl(net, "net", net_table);
-	if (!vzw_hdr)
-		pr_info("[mtk_net] register net sysctl optr is fail.\n");
+	/*
+	 * optr is one global (sysctl_optr), not per-namespace state, and
+	 * nothing would unregister a copy in another namespace: register it in
+	 * init_net only, which is never torn down.
+	 */
+	if (net_eq(net, &init_net)) {
+		vzw_hdr = register_net_sysctl(net, "net", net_table);
+		if (!vzw_hdr)
+			pr_info("[mtk_net] register net sysctl optr is fail.\n");
+	}
 
 	net->ipv6.sysctl.route_hdr =
 		register_net_sysctl(net, "net/ipv6/route", ipv6_route_table);
